    "java-ai": {
      "runner": "python sides/port_runner.py --which ai --variant published",
      "repo": "github.com/rcaran/hospice-cms-pricer-java, the published AI-assisted port (no licence file, GitHub API reports licenseInfo null; it ships .cursor/, .windsurf/ and .specs/ agent task files, so 'AI-assisted' is circumstantial, not declared)",
      "commit": "655847671859b67a188c5dae6a86c45a74bfa046",
      "licence": "none: fetched at run time at the pinned commit into cache/, never committed",
      "line": "FullPricerStrategy.java:79-86 a continuous-home-care day of less than 32 units is counted as a routine home care day (the two day counters are incremented, and the two flags that choose the return code are set), which HOSPR210.cbl's 2021-V210-CHC-0652 paragraph never does; PaymentCalculator.java:78-84 the CHC hourly rate is rounded half-up at 10 places, where the COBOL truncates",
      "source": "cache/repos/rcaran",
      "causes": [
        {
          "what": "a continuous-home-care day of less than 32 units is counted as a high-rate routine home care day; the CHC paragraph pays that day at an RHC rate but never touches the RHC day counters, which only the RHC paragraphs write",
          "port": "hospice-pricer-api/src/main/java/com/cms/hospice/pricing/FullPricerStrategy.java:79-80",
          "cobol": [
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6403-6422",
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6036",
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:5997"
          ],
          "fields": [
            "high",
            "low"
          ]
        },
        {
          "what": "the same short CHC day sets the flags that pick the return code, so a claim billing only continuous home care comes back 73 or 75 where the COBOL returns 00; the COBOL assigns 73/74/75/77 from the RHC day indicators alone",
          "port": "hospice-pricer-api/src/main/java/com/cms/hospice/pricing/FullPricerStrategy.java:79-86",
          "cobol": [
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6274-6312",
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6055",
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6018"
          ],
          "fields": [
            "rtc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "what": "the continuous-home-care hourly rate is rounded half-up at ten decimal places; the COBOL's arithmetic has no ROUNDED phrase on the intermediate divisions, so they truncate",
          "port": "hospice-pricer-api/src/main/java/com/cms/hospice/pricing/PaymentCalculator.java:78-84",
          "cobol": [
            "cache/cobol/HOSPR210.cbl:6430-6434",
